WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.004 --> 00:00:23.719
"I love Ally said the next morning, putting on her meld medallion.

2
00:00:23.739 --> 00:00:28.602
"It is illogical to love a day of the week," Alpha said.

3
00:00:28.622 --> 00:00:30.243
"You're right."

4
00:00:30.743 --> 00:00:31.304
Ally nodded.

5
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.341
"Except I always have Wednesdays off from work.

6
00:00:36.702 --> 00:00:37.983
That's the day that Dr.

7
00:00:38.023 --> 00:00:40.284
Lloyd's astronomy club meets at Ray's.

8
00:00:41.624 --> 00:00:43.905
The less I see him, the better!"

9
00:00:43.925 --> 00:00:47.287
"Correction," Alpha said.

10
00:00:47.307 --> 00:00:48.988
"That is logical."

11
00:00:49.008 --> 00:00:52.409
"You're working well today," Ally said.

12
00:00:52.429 --> 00:00:54.810
"I think I'll take you out with me."

13
00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:58.112
"Destination?" "Mateo's soccer camp.

14
00:00:58.956 --> 00:01:02.698
We're going to convince his coach to run an after-school soccer club."

15
00:01:02.718 --> 00:01:06.060
"You're using your Astral mind to help others."

16
00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:08.081
Alpha almost sounded proud.

17
00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:10.922
"That is a very Astralian thing to do."

18
00:01:17.226 --> 00:01:21.188
Ally and Mateo explained their idea to Coach Cross before camp began.

19
00:01:22.469 --> 00:01:24.090
"I love this idea!"

20
00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:25.330
Coach Cross said.

21
00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:28.312
"I miss coaching soccer during the school year.

22
00:01:29.076 --> 00:01:30.577
There's only one problem."

23
00:01:31.498 --> 00:01:33.020
"What?" Mateo asked.

24
00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.281
"How will we pay for it?

25
00:01:36.342 --> 00:01:39.285
I can't charge families the same price as I charge for camp.

26
00:01:40.246 --> 00:01:43.949
And I'd like to make it accessible to all kids, so the fees will need to be low."

27
00:01:43.969 --> 00:01:47.952
"Why does everything here have to cost money?"

28
00:01:48.393 --> 00:01:49.053
Ally asked.

29
00:01:49.073 --> 00:01:53.057
"Where I come from, all kids' activities are free."

30
00:01:53.077 --> 00:01:56.620
"Free?" Coach Cross gave her a surprised look.

31
00:01:57.408 --> 00:02:00.790
"I wish that's how it was here too, but we have to pay rent for the field, and

32
00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:06.993
buy equipment like soccer balls, cones, uniforms, nets "How much?"

33
00:02:07.433 --> 00:02:08.174
Mateo asked.

34
00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:12.136
"At least five hundred dollars," Coach said.

35
00:02:12.156 --> 00:02:15.958
"That's a lot."

36
00:02:17.659 --> 00:02:18.459
Mateo sighed.

37
00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.301
"Where are we going to get that much money?"

38
00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:28.488
Ally remembered what the waitress at Pepe's had told her when she first arrived on Earth: "If you

39
00:02:28.528 --> 00:02:31.930
want anything in this world, you've got to work for it."

40
00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:36.453
"I guess we'll have to work for it," Ally said.

41
00:02:36.473 --> 00:02:39.254
"You're right," Mateo said.

42
00:02:39.274 --> 00:02:41.276
"We can plan a fundraiser."

43
00:02:41.296 --> 00:02:45.398
"Interesting idea," Coach Cross said.

44
00:02:45.418 --> 00:02:46.859
"What will you sell?"

45
00:02:46.879 --> 00:02:52.862
"Maybe Randy from Ray's Diner can bake cupcakes," Mateo said.

46
00:02:52.882 --> 00:02:55.684
"And we can sell them from Papi's food truck.

47
00:02:57.216 --> 00:02:58.737
That should make us a lot of money."

48
00:02:58.757 --> 00:03:02.960
"Randy's cupcakes are so good," Ally said.

49
00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:10.425
"If we charge two dollars per cupcake, we'd have to sell 250 of them," Mateo said.

50
00:03:10.445 --> 00:03:12.867
"That should be pretty easy."

51
00:03:12.887 --> 00:03:16.430
"People do love cupcakes," Coach said.

52
00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:20.893
"Uh-oh!" Ally slapped her forehead.

53
00:03:20.913 --> 00:03:22.914
"I just remembered something.

54
00:03:23.394 --> 00:03:25.196
Randy is going on vacation soon.

55
00:03:25.792 --> 00:03:29.273
We can't ask him to make that many cupcakes before he leaves."

56
00:03:30.833 --> 00:03:35.175
"Well, it was a good idea, kids," Coach said.

57
00:03:35.195 --> 00:03:37.155
"Thanks for trying."

58
00:03:37.875 --> 00:03:41.076
Coach started to walk away when Ally noticed his T-shirt.

59
00:03:41.656 --> 00:03:45.017
It had the name of the soccer camp and a funny picture of a soccer ball.

60
00:03:45.037 --> 00:03:48.278
"Coach! Wait a minute!"

61
00:03:48.618 --> 00:03:49.098
she called.

62
00:03:49.798 --> 00:03:51.539
"What if we sell T-shirts?

63
00:03:52.059 --> 00:03:55.200
Do people love T-shirts as much as they love cupcakes?"

64
00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:57.061
Coach's eyes lit up.

65
00:03:57.741 --> 00:03:58.442
"They do!

66
00:04:00.664 --> 00:04:02.765
My twin brother owns the Sandville Print Shop.

67
00:04:03.265 --> 00:04:06.268
I can ask him to donate the printing if we can pay for the materials."

68
00:04:07.889 --> 00:04:10.771
Coach sent his brother a text, who replied right away.

69
00:04:10.791 --> 00:04:14.273
"Eli says he's happy to help.

70
00:04:14.814 --> 00:04:17.636
You can go see him at the shop after camp to discuss it with him."

71
00:04:19.657 --> 00:04:22.920
"We should ask Kate to design the shirt," Mateo said.

72
00:04:23.764 --> 00:04:26.765
"She told my mom she wants to be a fashion designer one day."

73
00:04:27.485 --> 00:04:30.206
Mateo texted Kate to ask her to help with the design.

74
00:04:31.706 --> 00:04:35.447
Ally and Mateo agreed to meet up again after camp to go to the print shop.

75
00:04:36.027 --> 00:04:39.308
Ally sighed with happiness after she waved good-bye to Mateo.

76
00:04:40.429 --> 00:04:44.070
"I'm so happy I can help him before I leave!"

77
00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:48.051
Ally spent the morning in the park.

78
00:04:50.211 --> 00:04:52.052
On her way home, she ran into Kate.

79
00:04:54.912 --> 00:04:59.235
"I was just going to text you and Mateo some T-shirt design ideas," Kate said.

80
00:05:00.135 --> 00:05:02.657
"Here, give me your phone, and I'll upload them for you."

81
00:05:03.617 --> 00:05:05.878
Ally nervously touched Alpha in her pocket.

82
00:05:05.898 --> 00:05:09.721
"Kate is always asking to see Alpha," Ally thought.

83
00:05:09.741 --> 00:05:14.283
"I can't let her, especially since Alpha still isn't working right."

84
00:05:14.303 --> 00:05:18.986
"Uh The fib popped out before Ally could stop herself.

85
00:05:19.006 --> 00:05:20.927
"I lost my phone."

86
00:05:22.524 --> 00:05:23.745
"That's terrible!"

87
00:05:24.165 --> 00:05:25.286
Kate looked horrified.

88
00:05:25.306 --> 00:05:28.229
"I can't imagine being without my phone!

89
00:05:28.789 --> 00:05:29.810
I'll help you find it."

90
00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:31.031
"That's okay.

91
00:05:31.051 --> 00:05:33.833
You don't have to—" Just then Kate's phone rang.

92
00:05:34.273 --> 00:05:35.074
"It's my mom.

93
00:05:35.394 --> 00:05:37.836
I have to take this call, but I'll see you later, Ally.

94
00:05:38.476 --> 00:05:40.618
Don't worry, we'll find your phone."

95
00:05:40.638 --> 00:05:43.480
"No, really, please don't worry about it!"

96
00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:44.441
Ally said.

97
00:05:44.681 --> 00:05:48.244
But Kate had already walked off, her phone pressed to her ear.
